  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan Angels</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Sudan, entrepreneurship is an important mechanism to realise increases in aggregate well-being. For entrepreneurship to flourish, young entrepreneurs need to be able to start their companies and attract the right capital to grow their company.Angel investors can play a key and formative role in the development of young start-up companies. They can invest their finance, knowledge, networks, and access to markets into these young and aspiring entrepreneurs. This can have a catalytic effect and grow the young company exponentially. In doing so, the company is able to offer innovative products and services that are needed locally, while creating jobs and growing the local economy. Angel investors also have an emancipating role in their local ecosystems. They have been successful themselves and are now ready to give back to their communities. This will result in a more active ecosystem that seizes opportunities and becomes a better pipeline of support for the next generation of trailblazers. Indeed, angel investors put the fun back in fundamental change.This African Angel Academy is able to grow the capacity of both the Business Angel Networks as their member angel investors.</narrative>
  </description>
